  "raw_text": "83\n\n(Note/Nota: It is similar to the\n \nCreole\n:\n \nMek wi...\n \n/ Es similar a la criollo\n:\n \nMek wi...\n)\n\nKaisa aisi kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nlet’s go to\n \nread\n \n/ vamos a leer\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nKaisa baiki sakanka 5 ba aisi kaikaia\n \n–\n \nLet’s go to read\n \nparagraph 5\n \n/ Vamos a leer el párrafo 5\n)\n\nKaisa dans pulaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nlet’s dance\n \n/ vamos a bailar\n\nKaisa kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nlet’s\n \nsee\n \n/ veamos\n\nKaisa laki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nlet’s examine\n \n/ examinemos\n\nKaisa lan takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nlet’s learn\n \n/ aprendamos\n\nKaisa kau\n \nlan takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nlet’s learn more\n \n/ aprendamos más\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nyc8\n):\n \nKaisa kau lan\n \ntakaia Josías bara ai pânika yamni nani brin ba du\nkiara.\n \n–\n \nLet’s learn more\n\nabout Josiah and the good friends he had.\n \n/ Aprendamos más sobre Josías y los buenos amigos que\n\ntuvo.\n)\n\nKaisa waia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nlet’s go\n \n/ vamonos\n\nKaisma\n \n(v-2p-fut-I of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nyou will be, you will imminently be, you will immediately be\n \n/ serás, serás\ninminentemente, serás inmediatamente\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmy59\n):\n \nNa tihmia mahka was, apia sa kaka yauhka pat pruram kaisma.\n \n–\n \nTonight go right away, otherwise,\n\ntomorrow you will be dead.\n \n/ Esta noche ve de inmediato, de lo contrario, mañana estarás muerto.\n)\n\nKaisna\n \n(v-1p-fut-I of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nI will be, I will imminently be, I will immediately be, I will now be\n \n/ seré, estaré,\nestaré inminentemente, estaré inmediatamente, ahora estaré\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Yamni Kulki Lawana 3:21\n):\n \ndiara kum baman kupi ra bri kaisna\n \n–\n \nI will now be having only one thing in my heart\n \n/\nAhora solo tendré una cosa en mi corazón)\n\nKakaira kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto know, to be acquainted\n \n/ conocer, estar familiarizado\n\nKama\n \n(v-2p-fut of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(\nyou) will be\n \n/ (tú) serás\n\nKamna\n \n(v-1p-fut of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(I) will be\n \n/ seré\n\nKan\n \n(v-3p-past/pasado II of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nwas, were\n \n/ era\n\nBri kan\n \n–\n \nwas having, had been\n \n/ estaba teniendo, había estado\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nyc-8\n):\n \n8 mani baman bri kan!\n \n–\n \n(He) was (having) just 8 years!\n \n/ (Él) tenía solo 8 años!)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb86\n):\n \nJisas Betania ra wan taim, Lasarus bikan yu walhwal bri kan\n \n–\n \nWhen Jesus went to Bethany, Lazurus\nhad been buried for 4 days\n \n/ Cuando Jesús fue a Betania, Lázaro había estado enterrado por 4 días)\n\nKan kaia sa\n \n–\n \nmust have been, must have been the case\n \n/ debe haber sido, debe haber sido el caso\n\nKapara\n \n(v-proh of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \ndon’t be\n \n/ no seas\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Sins Lâka 3:5\n):\n \nman sinskam lâka ba kat tniwi kapara\n \n–\n \ndon’t be leaning/trusting on your own wisdom\n \n/ no te\napoyes/confíes en tu propia sabiduría)\n\nKapram\n \n(v-2p-past/pasado-II of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(you) were\n \n/ eras\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n: In Honduras, pronounced\n \nKaram\n \n/ En Honduras, pronunciado\n \nKaram\n)\n\nKapras\n \n(v\n-\nneg\n \nof\n/de\n:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nnot be\n \n/ no ser\n/estar\n\nKapri\n \n(\nv\n-\n1p\n-\npast\n/pasado\n-\nII of\n/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(I) was\n \n/\n \n(Yo) estaba\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n: In Honduras, pronounced\n \nKari\n \n/ En Honduras, pronunciado\n \nKari\n)\n\nKata\n \n(v-3p-past/pasado-I of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nwas, were\n \n/ era\n\nKatma\n \n(v-2p-past/pasado-I of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(you) were\n \n/ eras\n\nKatna\n \n(v-1p-past/pasado-I of/de:\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \n(I) was\n \n/ (Yo) estaba\n\nLilia kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be happy, to be joyful\n \n/ ser feliz, ser alegre\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfg9\n):\n \nJehova want sa luhpa nani ba lilia kabia\n \n–\n \nJehovah wants children to be happy\n \n/ Jehová quiere que los niños\nsean felices)\n\nSi\n \n(v\n-\npresent\n \nparticiple\n \nof the verb\n \nKaia\n \n/\n \nparticipio presente\n \ndel verbo\n \nKaia\n)\n \n–\n \nbeing\n, is being\n \n/ siendo\n, esta\n\nsiendo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh164\n):\n \nKarnika sut bri Papaskra pali ba, wan lamara si, wan walbia\n \n–\n \nThe almighty Creator\n \nbeing close to\n \nus\n,\n \nwill\n\nhear us\n \n/ El todopoderoso Creador\n \nsiendo\n \ncerca de nosotros\n, n\nos escuchará\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n03/19\n):\n \nMan nu\n \nâ\npu si upla kum ra saura munram kaka, …\n \n–\n \nIf you hurt a person\n \nnot\n \nbeing aware of\n \nit\n,\n \n…\n \n/ Si\n\nlastimas a una persona\n \nno\n \nsiendo consciente de e\nll\no, …)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n08/19\n):\n \nWan dara walras si muni nahki sip sa p\nâ\nna saura nani wal taukaia?\n \n–\n \nWithout our being aware, how is\n\nit possible to travel (associate) with bad friends?\n \n/\n \nSin\n \nque seamos\n \nconsciente\ns\n,\n \ncómo es posible\n \nand\nar (asociarse) con\n\nmalos amigos?\n)\n\nBan kra si\n \n–\n \nmaybe it is the case, maybe it is being the case, maybe so\n \n/ tal vez sea el\n \ncas\no\n, tal vez\n \nsiendo\n\nel caso, tal vez",
